From: Project Luma diagnostics <diagnostics@project-luma.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a810: use the Gen8.3 GMU boot rate

Fairphone's published Gen8.3 driver selects the upper GMU power level,
650 MHz, before releasing CM3 reset. The generic DRM/MSM path requests
200 MHz, which rounds to the A810 device tree's lower 350 MHz OPP.

Use the stock Gen8.3 boot rate for A810 only. Keep every other A8xx and
the later firmware-managed frequency table unchanged.

This is a one-variable behavior test. It must be applied after the A810
timeout diagnostics and without the rejected AHB fence-range patch.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1315,7 +1315,8 @@ static int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	a6xx_gmu_gxpd_get(gmu);
 
 	/* Use a known rate to bring up the GMU */
-	clk_set_rate(gmu->core_clk, 200000000);
+	clk_set_rate(gmu->core_clk,
+		     adreno_is_a810(adreno_gpu) ? 650000000 : 200000000);
 	clk_set_rate(gmu->hub_clk, adreno_is_a740_family(adreno_gpu) ?
 		     200000000 : 150000000);
 	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(gmu->nr_clocks, gmu->clocks);
-- 
2.50.1
